# Netlify's own internal paths (/.netlify/functions/*, etc.) are reserved
# at the platform level - Netlify won't even accept a _redirects rule
# whose "from" pattern starts with /.netlify (confirmed: it rejects that
# syntax outright at deploy time), and empirically, requests to the
# signup function below still reach the function's own code and logic
# with the catch-all rule in place. No passthrough rule is needed or
# possible here.

# Catch-all for every future partner (Phase 3): a partner created through
# the signup function has no physical file at all, so once Netlify has
# confirmed no real file/path matches - which happens before any
# _redirects rule is even consulted - this is the only thing left that
# can match, and it always resolves to the same dynamic template. Not
# forced: there is nothing to force it over except the explicit slugs
# above (already forced), /assets/*, /partner/*, and / itself, all of
# which are real files/paths and are matched before this line is ever
# reached.
